UPDATE companies SET description='Baltimore Aircoil Company (BAC) was founded in 1938 in Milford, Delaware. The company began with a single revolutionary cooling coil hand-built in the founder''s garage. Today it is employee-owned, with more than 2,000 team members worldwide.

BAC designs and manufactures cooling equipment including evaporative condensers, adiabatic coolers, modular hybrid coolers, and water treatment systems for comfort cooling, process cooling, and refrigeration applications. Recent introductions such as the Trillium™ Adiabatic Cooler TRFS for large-scale data centers and the Nexus® Modular Hybrid Cooler with PuriStream™ water treatment illustrate the company''s focus on hybrid and adiabatic technology. The company employs over 2,000 people globally and operates on nearly every continent.

BAC serves heavy industrial and energy sectors, as well as large-scale data center operators. Its equipment is used in demanding environments requiring high-capacity cooling and refrigeration, and the company provides parts and inspection services to support installed units throughout their lifecycle.

BAC differentiates itself through a partnership model that spans the full equipment lifecycle, a focus on sustainable cooling that balances water and energy savings, and an employee-ownership culture that drives long-term customer relationships. The company states its mission is to continually advance truly sustainable cooling inspired by nature and powered by its people.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Comfort cooling system design", "Process cooling system design", "Refrigeration system design", "Evaporative condenser manufacturing", "Adiabatic cooler manufacturing", "Modular hybrid cooler manufacturing", "Water treatment system integration", "Parts supply and inspection", "Equipment lifecycle support"], "industries": ["Heavy industrial", "Energy", "Data centers"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Trillium\u2122 Adiabatic Cooler TRFS", "Nexus\u00ae Modular Hybrid Cooler", "PuriStream\u2122 Water Treatment System", "Evaporative Condenser"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned culture with 2,000+ global team members", "Full lifecycle partnership from initial design through installed equipment support", "Sustainable cooling technology balancing water and energy savings", "Global reach with local representative network", "Innovation in adiabatic and hybrid cooling systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1938 -> /about", "Headquarters Milford, Delaware -> db", "Employee-owned -> /about", "2,000+ global employees -> /about", "Manufactures evaporative condensers, adiabatic coolers, hybrid coolers -> /about, /", "Serves heavy industrial & energy -> /", "Serves data centers -> / (news)", "Partnership lifecycle approach -> /about", "Sustainability focus on water and energy savings -> /about", "Trillium Adiabatic Cooler TRFS -> /", "Nexus Modular Hybrid Cooler -> /", "PuriStream Water Treatment System -> /", "Employee-owners culture -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "BAC creates sustainable comfort cooling, process cooling, and refrigeration solutions for the most essential and demanding environments on earth.", "founded_year": "1938", "employee_count": "2,000+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/baltimore-aircoil-company/"], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='baltimore-aircoil-company-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BAPKO Metal Inc. is headquartered in Orange, California, with additional production facilities in San Diego. The company was founded in 1978 as a partnership and operated as a family-owned business for 28 years before transitioning to single ownership. In its 41st year, 2019, BAPKO became 100% employee-owned, a structure the firm says provides financial resilience and a family-centric culture.

The company self-performs miscellaneous steel and architectural metal fabrication and installation. Its original 13,000-square-foot shop in Orange has grown to more than 55,000 square feet across multiple buildings, including over 33,000 square feet of dedicated fabrication space. Services span estimating, design assist, BIM modeling with Tekla Structures, 3D laser scanning, project management, production, and field installation. Two divisions — Miscellaneous Metals and Architectural Metals — work with carbon steel, stainless steel, bronze, aluminum, and glass.

BAPKO serves general contractors, architects, and engineers on commercial, healthcare, educational, and industrial projects throughout Southern California, from San Diego to Palo Alto. Notable projects include the Gaylord Pacific Resort & Convention Center in Chula Vista, the Intuit Dome (Clippers Arena) in Inglewood, and the Din Tai Fung restaurant at Downtown Disney in Anaheim.

The firm emphasizes an all-in-one, self-performing model that controls quality and schedule from concept through installation. Employee ownership is cited as a driver of financial stability and team retention, while investments in BIM and laser-scanning technology aim to reduce field conflicts and accelerate timelines. Safety is managed through dedicated professionals and union ironworkers (Locals 433 and 229).', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Estimating", "Design Assist", "BIM Modeling (Tekla Structures)", "3D Laser Scanning", "Project Management", "Structural Steel Fabrication", "Architectural Metal Fabrication", "Glass Fabrication", "Installation"], "industries": ["Commercial Construction", "Healthcare Construction", "Educational Construction", "Industrial Construction", "Hospitality", "Entertainment", "Retail"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Bronze", "Aluminum", "Glass"], "equipment": ["Tekla Structures BIM software", "Lidar 3D laser scanner"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% employee-owned since 2019", "Self-performing fabrication and installation under one roof", "Over 55,000 sq ft of fabrication and office space in Southern California", "In-house BIM modeling with Tekla Structures and 3D laser scanning", "Union ironworker installation crews (Locals 433 & 229)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1978 -> db, /about", "Headquartered in Orange, CA -> db, /about", "100% Employee Owned since 2019 -> /, /about", "Original 13,000 sq ft shop, expanded to over 55,000 sq ft -> /about", "Over 33,000 sq ft fabrication space -> /services", "Services: Estimating, Design Assist, BIM, Project Management, Production, Installation -> /services", "Miscellaneous Metals and Architectural Metals divisions -> /about", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, bronze, aluminum, glass -> /about", "Industries: commercial, healthcare, educational, industrial -> /about", "Projects: Gaylord Pacific Resort, Intuit Dome, Din Tai Fung -> /", "Tekla Structures BIM software -> /services", "Lidar 3D laser scanner -> /services", "Ironworkers Local 433 & 229 -> /services", "Self-performing contractor -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "BAPKO Metal Inc. is a self-performing contractor specializing in miscellaneous steel and architectural metal fabrication and installation.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bapko-metal-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Barber Packaging Company was established in 1989 in Bangor, Michigan, as a family-owned and operated business. The company has remained under family ownership for more than 35 years, building its reputation on long-term customer partnerships.

The company provides engineered packaging solutions across five categories: returnable packaging made from steel, wood, plastics, textiles, and foam; expendable one-way packaging for export, service, backup, and retail; work-in-progress (WIP) intra-plant material handling systems; service and backup packaging to OEM specifications; and export packaging designed for sea containers and intermodal transport. Barber’s in-house design team uses CAD to create 3D models from customer data, and its rapid prototyping service delivers form-fit-test-review cycles. A manufacturing floor described as one of the industry’s most capable produces custom protective packaging, while validation and testing—including shake and drop tests performed with accredited labs—ensure compliance. Program management covers design concept through system fills.

Barber serves a range of industries that require protective packaging, with specific references to assembly plants and OEM supply chains.

The company differentiates itself through what it calls “The Barber Way”—a relationship-based approach that emphasizes consistency, collaboration, and single-source coordination. Customers cite faster turnaround times, cost savings, and simplified project management as key reasons for partnering with Barber.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CAD Design & Engineering", "Rapid Prototyping (form, fit, test, review)", "Custom Protective Packaging Manufacturing", "Shake and Drop Testing", "Accredited Lab Validation", "Program Management", "Returnable Packaging Design", "Expendable Packaging Design", "Work-In-Progress (WIP) Packaging Design", "Service/Backup Packaging Design", "Export Packaging Design"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Steel", "Wood", "Plastics", "Textiles", "Foam", "Corrugated", "Plastic Corrugated"], "equipment": ["CNC Abrasive Wire", "CNC Oscillating and Tangential", "Automated Assembly"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service approach from design through program management", "In-house CAD design and rapid prototyping", "Manufacturing floor focused on shortened lead times", "Validation & testing with accredited labs", "Relationship-based model with long-term partnerships"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 -> db", "Headquarters in Bangor, Michigan -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> db, home page", "Full-service approach for custom protective packaging -> home page", "In-house design team utilizes CAD technology -> home page", "Rapid prototyping services with form fit, testing, review -> home page", "Manufacturing floor with shortened lead times -> home page", "Validation & testing with accredited labs and shake/drop testing -> home page", "Program management from design concept to system fills -> home page", "Returnable packaging from steel, wood, plastics, textiles, foam -> home page", "Expendable packaging for export, service, backup, retail -> home page", "WIP intra-plant material 