UPDATE companies SET description='Bardot Plastics operates from a modern facility in Easton, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1973 by J. Lee Boucher, the company began as a vision to provide superior injection molding services and has since grown into a third-generation, family-owned business now led by Chris, Jim, and Rick Boucher.

The company specializes in high-tonnage injection molding, with presses up to 1,760 tons capable of producing large, complex parts that many molders cannot accommodate. Its full-service offering spans design consultation, integrated tooling (single-cavity, multi-cavity, and family molds), insert molding, sonic welding, in-house assembly, packaging, and fulfillment. A 120-ton central chilling unit and advanced robotics support consistent quality across runs.

Bardot serves a diverse industrial base including office furniture, lawn and garden, waste and recycling, industrial equipment, military, construction, agricultural, and commercial markets.

The founding mantra “making it right the first time” drives the operation, guided by principles of excellence, innovation, sustainability, and partnership. The company differentiates itself through large-tonnage capacity, end-to-end single-source solutions, dedicated project managers, and continuous investment in technology such as the recent chilling unit installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (high-tonnage up to 1,760 tons)", "Large part molding", "Integrated tooling design and manufacturing", "Insert molding", "Sonic welding", "Post-molding assembly", "In-house assembly", "Packaging and fulfillment", "Design consultation", "Quality assurance and control", "Robotics-assisted production"], "industries": ["Office Furniture", "Lawn & Garden", "Waste & Recycling", "Industrial", "Military", "Construction", "Agricultural", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Engineered resins", "Non-engineered resins"], "equipment": ["1,760-ton injection molding presses", "120-ton central chilling unit", "Advanced robotics for part removal"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["High-tonnage molding up to 1,760 tons with full robotic part removal", "Integrated tooling design and build (single-cavity, multi-cavity, family molds)", "Insert molding and sonic welding/post-molding assembly", "In-house assembly, packaging, and domestic/international fulfillment", "Dedicated project managers as single point of contact from concept to delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1973 by J. Lee Boucher -> /about", "Third-generation family-owned, led by Chris, Jim, and Rick Boucher -> /about", "Headquarters in Easton, Pennsylvania -> /, /about", "High-tonnage molding up to 1,760 tons -> /, /capabilities", "Full robotic part removal -> /capabilities", "Integrated tooling capabilities (single-cavity, multi-cavity, family molds) -> /capabilities", "Insert molding and sonic welding/post-molding assembly -> /capabilities", "In-house 