UPDATE companies SET description='Bayatronics was founded in 2021 in Concord, North Carolina, with a second location in Richardson, Texas. The company was established by Dirk Warriner, who serves as CEO and brings 41 years of experience in electronic manufacturing. The management team collectively holds over 40 years of experience in PCBA and electro‑mechanical sub‑assemblies at Tier 1 contract manufacturers and OEMs in industrial and medical fields. The founders were motivated by lessons learned from participating in the Malcolm Baldrige National Quality Award competition, which they won twice, and aimed to provide domestic customers with high‑volume, cost‑competitive solutions with superior quality.

Bayatronics operates as an electronic manufacturing services (EMS) provider specializing in printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), design for manufacturability (DFM), final assembly, and logistics. The company runs surface‑mount technology (SMT) lines equipped with Juki RS‑1R pick‑and‑place machines, Juki G‑Titan solder paste printers, CyberOptics SPI and AOI systems, Juki iCUBE selective soldering, and Seica Pilot V8 flying probe and in‑circuit testers. The team reports 208 years of combined experience.

The company serves industrial, instrumentation, transportation, medical device, cable manufacturing, and consumer electronics sectors. Customers include OEMs and innovators in advanced fields such as cell therapy, gene therapy, and antibody development, as well as companies like Smart Level (referenced in a testimonial). Bayatronics emphasizes 100% U.S.‑based operations and full transparency in cost and quality.

Bayatronics differentiates itself through day‑of response to customer inquiries, quotes within five working days, and a commitment to integrity standards with open‑book pricing. The company pursues continuous improvement, cutting‑edge technology, and a dedicated team to support customers in creating reliable, efficient electronic products. Its quality system adheres to IPC 610, ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, and RoHS compliance, with AS9100 certification in progress.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','AS9100 (in progress)','RoHS','IPC 610']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM)", "New Product Introduction (NPI) support", "Final Assembly (mechanical assembly, functional testing)", "Conformal Coating", "Electromechanical Assembly", "Solder Paste Inspection (SPI)", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "X\u2011Ray Inspection", "Flying Probe Testing", "In\u2011Circuit Testing", "Selective Soldering", "Reflow Soldering", "Material Management / Logistics", "Inventory Control (MRP)", "Global Procurement", "Failure Analysis", "Repair / ECO", "Pre\u2011Assembly Assessments", "Turn\u2011Key Open Book Pricing"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Instrumentation", "Transportation", "Medical Device", "Cable Manufacturing", "Consumer Electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Juki ISM3600", "Juki ISM500", "Juki G\u2011Titan", "Cyber Optics SE500 Ultra", "Juki RS\u20111R", "Juki Reflow Oven (8 zones + 2 zones)", "Cyber Optics SQ3000", "Juki iCUBE", "Seica Pilot V8 Next Series"], "volume": "Prototype to medium\u2011volume production", "lead_time": "Quotes within 5 business days; manufacturing cycle time customized per project", "tolerances": "\u00b135 \u00b5m placement accuracy (CPK \u22651)", "built_on": ["Same\u2011day customer response via email, text, or phone", "Quotes delivered within five business days", "Open\u2011book pricing with full cost transparency", "100% U.S.\u2011based 