UPDATE companies SET description='Behlen Mfg. Co. traces its roots to a garage in Columbus, Nebraska, where it was founded in 1936. Over the decades the company has grown into a multi‑unit enterprise with operations spanning five states, while keeping its headquarters in Columbus.

The company operates through distinct business units that design and manufacture a range of steel‑based products. A dedicated transportation arm, BMC Transportation, runs a flatbed fleet serving 48 U.S. states and Canadian provinces. The firm emphasizes lean manufacturing and a quality program called PRIDE that authorizes any employee to stop a process that falls short of specifications.

The company cites its 85‑plus years of experience, integrated product lines, and in‑house transportation as reasons customers choose it.

Behlen says its differentiation lies in its PRIDE quality culture, multiple facility certifications (IAS and AISC), and a commitment to sustainable steel use. The company’s stated purpose is to deliver high‑quality products that strengthen the industries it serves, while empowering its workforce—referred to as Partners in Progress—through shared values and variable pay.', certifications=ARRAY['IAS','AISC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal building systems manufacturing", "Grain storage system manufacturing", "Livestock equipment manufacturing", "Custom metal fabrication", "Coil stitching equipment manufacturing", "Capacitor winding machine manufacturing", "Flatbed transportation services", "Quality assurance (PRIDE system)", "Lean manufacturing"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Construction", "Grain storage", "Energy", "Transportation"], "materials": ["Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["85+ years of manufacturing experience", "Dedicated flatbed fleet covering 48 U.S. states and Canadian provinces", "IAS and AISC certified facilities", "PRIDE quality system giving every employee authority to halt non\u2011conforming work", "Integrated product lines spanning metal buildings, grain storage, custom fabrication, and capacitor winding equipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1936 in a Columbus, Nebraska garage -> /about", "Headquarters at 4025 E. 23rd St., Columbus, Nebraska -> /", "Operations across five states -> /about", "Business units: Behlen Building Systems, Behlen Grain Systems, Behlen Country, Behlen Custom Fabrication, Behlen Joiner, Hilton Behlen Energy Systems, BMC Transportation -> /", "Products: metal building systems, livestock equipment, grain storage systems, strip joiners, capacitor winding machines -> /", "Dedicated transportation across 48 states and Canadian provinces -> /", "Quality certifications: IAS (Columbus), IAS and AISC (Sarasota) -> /", "PRIDE quality system with employee authority to stop non-conforming processes -> /", "Lean manufacturing and AIM program -> /about", "Leadership: Tony Raimondo Jr. (Board Chair), Tom Boal (President & CEO), Brad Robeson (COO), Craig Fitzpatrick (CFO), Farshad Vossoughi (VP & CIO) -> /about", "Sustainability: products predominantly made of steel, most recycled material -> /about", "Mission, Vision, Purpose statements -> /about", "Global values: Safety, Quality, Productivity, Teamwork, Communication, Honor System, Sharing & Variable Pay, Continuous Learning, Continuous Improvement, Customer Satisfaction -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our diverse line of products, from metal building systems to livestock equipment, grain storage systems, strip joiners, and capacitor winding machines, reflect our commitment to excellence and reliability.", "founded_year": "1936", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='behlen-mfg-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Belden is headquartered in St. Louis, Missouri. The company traces its origins to 1902 when the Belden Manufacturing Company was incorporated with Joe Belden as president and Albert Beutler as plant superintendent. The business began producing wire and cable products that would later support early radio, television, and wartime communications.

Today Belden manufactures cables and connectivity solutions for industrial and networking applications. Its portfolio includes industrial Ethernet and fiber optic cables, as well as complete connection solutions that span from the factory floor to the data center. The company reports a global workforce of 8 employees and operates across 18 countries certified as Great Place to Work locations.

Belden serves customers in consumer packaged goods, data centers, energy, hospitality, mass transit, and warehousing and logistics. In each sector the company provides wired and wireless infrastructure that connects sensors, machines, control systems, and enterprise networks. It also offers network design, installation, hypercare, and run-and-maintain services to support deployment and ongoing operations.

The company states that it exists to bridge the gap between lost signals, security breaches, and disparate networks, turning those challenges into opportunities for clarity and innovation. Belden emphasizes its unified approach—integrating products, services, and partner ecosystems—to deliver complete connection solutions. Its history of firsts, such as bringing industrial Ethernet to market in the early 1980s and supplying cable for the Apollo 11 mission, underscores its focus on enabling critical connectivity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable manufacturing", "Connectivity solutions", "Industrial Ethernet cabling", "Fiber optic cabling", "Network design services", "Network installation services", "Hypercare services", "Run and maintain services"], "industries": ["Consumer Packaged Goods", "Data Centers", "Energy", "Hospitality", "Mass Transit", "Warehousing & Logistics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First to market industrial Ethernet and fiber optic cables (early 1980s)", "Cable used on Apollo 11 mission", "Supplier for Olympic broadcasts for over 20 years", "Unified \"complete connection solutions\" approach integrating products and services", "120-year history of innovation in wire and cable"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1902 -> db", "Headquarters St. Louis, Missouri -> db", "Manufactures cables and connectivity solutions -> db description", "Industries served: Consumer Packaged Goods, Data Centers, Energy, Hospitality, Mass Transit, Warehousing & Logistics -> /", "Services: Design, Install, Hypercare, Run & Maintain -> /services", "Founders: Joe Belden (president), Albert Beutler (plant superintendent) -> /about-us", "First to market industrial Ethernet and fiber optic cables (early 1980s) -> /about-us", "Acquisitions: PPC, Hirschmann, ProSoft Technology -> /about-us", "120 years of innovation -> /about-us", "8 Employees globally -> /about-us", "18 Great Place to Work Certified countries -> /about-us", "Why we exist statement -> /about-us", "Unified approach/complete connection solutions -> /about-us", "Cable used on Apollo 11 -> /about-us", "Olympic broadcast supplier for over 20 years -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufactures cables and connectivity solutions for industrial and networking applications.", "founded_year": "1902", "employee_count": "8 Employees globally", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='belden' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bell Semiconductor is based in Chicago, Illinois. The company traces its lineage to the intellectual property portfolio that originated at Bell Labs following the invention of the transistor. That portfolio passed through Lucent Technologies, Agere Systems, LSI, Avago, and Broadcom before becoming the foundation of Bell Semiconductor. Key leaders include Chad Hilyard and Sailesh Merchant, both of whom previously held leadership roles in the intellectual property businesses at Lucent, Agere Systems, and LSI.

Bell Semiconductor licenses a semiconductor intellectual property portfolio that covers technologies enabling continued integration of semiconductor devices. The portfolio is licensed to virtually all foundries and integrated device manufacturers, supporting production of smartphones, PCs, tablets, wearables, and IoT devices.

Its customers span the semiconductor manufacturing industry, including foundries and integrated device manufacturers that produce chips for consumer electronics, mobile communications, and internet-of-things markets. Licensees include major players in the smartphone, PC, tablet, wearable, and IoT device sectors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Intellectual property licensing", "Semiconductor patent portfolio administration", "Technology transfer"], "industries": ["Semiconductor manufacturing", "Foundries", "Integrated device manufacturers", "Smartphones", "PCs", "Tablets", "Wearables", "IoT devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Successor to the Bell Labs transistor patent portfolio", "Portfolio licensed to virtually all foundries and integrated device manufacturers", "Leadership with deep IP experience at Lucent, Agere Systems, and LSI"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Chicago, Illinois -> db", "Successor to Bell Labs transistor IP portfolio -> /", "Portfolio licensed to virtually all foundries and integrated device manufacturers -> /", "Key leaders: Chad Hilyard and Sailesh Merchant -> /", "Leaders previously held IP leadership roles at Lucent, Agere Systems, LSI -> /", "Technologies enable smartphones, PCs, tablets, wearables, IoT devices -> /", "Contact: Lynn Wilson, ,  -> /", "Address: 401 N. Michigan Ave., Chicago, IL 60611 -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Bell Semiconductor is the successor in interest to the intellectual property portfolio that originated at Bell Labs following the invention of the transistor.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bell-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bellisio Foods, Inc. operates from Jackson, Ohio, where it produces frozen meals for retail brands and contract-manufacturing partners. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but its history traces back to early quality practices attributed to an individual named Jeno, who conducted taste tests that shaped its quality-assurance culture.

The company runs full-scale production facilities that handle component processing, manufacturing, cooling, freezing, warehousing, and storage, turning out more than two million meals each day. A dedicated culinary center supports product development, where food scientists and chefs create new recipes and custom formulations for both Bellisio''s own brands and partner labels. Services span research and development, commercialization support, and contract manufacturing.

