UPDATE companies SET description='Berne Apparel is headquartered in Ossian, Indiana, and traces its roots to 1915 when it began making bib overalls and work shirts for the farming community in Berne, Indiana.

The brand designs and sells a range of workwear including insulated bib overalls, coveralls, jackets, pants, tees, vests, hooded sweatshirts, and UPF-rated sun shirts. Each insulated garment carries a proprietary warmth rating—Warm, Warmer, Warmest, or Extreme Warmth—to help buyers match protection to conditions. Sizing runs from small to 6XL in short, regular, and tall lengths, with a dedicated women’s line (S–4XL) built for female proportions and a big-and-tall offering across nine sizes and three lengths. Through its Berne ProGear program, the company also provides custom printing and embroidery for businesses wanting branded apparel.

Customers span individual tradespeople—farmers, linemen, roofers, and outdoor workers in regions like the Catskills and Iowa—as well as corporate buyers ordering logoed gear for crews. The company highlights real-world use cases from a lineman in Iowa and a small-farm family in New York.

Berne positions itself on delivering “workwear as good as the big guys, at a price hardworking people can actually pay.” Its differentiators include the multi-generation family ownership, the warmth-rating system, women’s-specific patterning, extended sizing, and the ProGear customization service, all backed by free shipping on orders over $100.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Workwear design and manufacturing", "Custom apparel decoration (screen printing, embroidery)", "Warmth rating classification", "Extended size grading (including big & tall and women''s fits)"], "industries": ["Agriculture/Farming", "Construction", "Utilities", "Outdoor Recreation", "Corporate Branded Apparel", "General Workwear"], "materials": ["Duck canvas", "Washed duck", "Ripstop fabric", "Thermal lining", "Insulation", "UPF-rated fabric"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family owned since 1915, now in its third generation", "Proprietary warmth rating system (Warm, Warmer, Warmest, Extreme Warmth) on every insulated piece", "Extended sizing: S\u20136XL in short, regular, and tall; women\u2019s S\u20134XL; big & tall across nine sizes and three lengths", "Women\u2019s workwear built for female proportions, not adapted from men\u2019s patterns", "Berne ProGear custom printing and embroidery for corporate logos", "Free shipping on orders over $100"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1915 in Berne, Indiana -> /", "Family-owned, three generations -> /", "Headquarters in Ossian, Indiana -> db", "Produces workwear: bibs, coveralls, jackets, pants, tees, vests, sweatshirts, sun shirts -> /", "Warmth rating system (Warm, Warmer, Warmest, Extreme Warmth) -> /", "Extended sizing S-6XL, short/regular/tall, women''s S-4XL, big & tall -> /", "Berne ProGear custom printing/embroidery for corporate logos -> /", "Free shipping on orders $100+ -> /", "Materials: duck canvas, washed duck, ripstop, thermal lining, insulation, UPF fabric -> /", "Serves farm community, linemen, roofers, outdoor workers, corporate clients -> /", "Company type: Manufacturer -> /", "Makes products: yes -> /", "Ownership: Family-owned -> /", "Social: Instagram @berneapparel -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Berne started making bibs and work shirts for the farm community in Berne, Indiana.", "founded_year": "1915", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.instagram.com/berneapparel/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='berne-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bernhaus Furniture is a family-owned furniture retailer based in Berne, Indiana, a town with Swiss roots reflected in the company’s name and bear logo. The business opened its doors in 2003 with a simple premise: choosing furniture should feel personal. From its showroom in Berne, the company serves homeowners throughout the region.

The retailer curates American-made, Amish-crafted furniture for dining rooms, bedrooms, living rooms, offices, children’s rooms, and outdoor spaces. Beyond stock pieces, Bernhaus offers a guided customization process where customers can specify dimensions, wood species, stain colors, and hardware, or submit drawings and inspiration photos for fully custom work. The company handles delivery, assembly, and in-home setup, and notes that custom orders typically require about 12 weeks to complete.

Its showroom provides free walk-in design assistance, and the company emphasizes a low-pressure buying experience with transparent pricing based on materials, size, finish, and options selected.

Bernhaus highlights three guiding principles: practical service from concept through installation, fair value without unnecessary complexity, and the ability to tailor each piece to the customer’s space and taste.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Furniture retail", "Custom furniture specification", "Design consultation", "Delivery and assembly", "In-home setup"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Wood", "Stain", "Hardware"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Approximately 12 weeks for custom pieces", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Expert showroom guidance through delivery, assembly, and in-home setup", "Transparent pricing based on materials, size, finish, and options", "Customization of size, wood, stain, and hardware", "Custom pieces typically completed in approximately 12 weeks", "Free walk-in design help in showroom"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2003 -> db, /about", "Family-owned -> /, /about", "Headquartered in Berne, Indiana -> /, /about", "Sells Amish-crafted furniture -> /", "Offers customization of size, wood, stain, hardware -> /", "Provides delivery, assembly, and in-home setup -> /", "Custom pieces typically completed in approximately 12 weeks -> /", "Free walk-in design help in showroom -> /", "Company name derives from Swiss word ''Bern'' meaning bear -> /about", "Guiding principles: service, fair value, customization -> /about"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Bernhaus is a family-owned furniture store in Berne, Indiana", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bernhaus-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Best Wire & Cable was established in 2004 in Richardson, Texas, by industry veteran Joe Stadelman, who serves as president. The company began with a "Customer First" philosophy and has grown into a nationwide distributor of wire and cable products.

The company operates as a wire and cable distributor, supplying products ranging from service entrance and multi-conductor cables to specialty Mil-Spec, aerospace, and shipboard cables. Its Dallas, Texas warehouse supports same-day shipping on stocked items, and the firm reports distributing more than 300 million feet of wire annually across over 100,000 projects.

Best Wire & Cable serves customers in aerospace, shipboard, and defense sectors requiring Mil-Spec cables, as well as commercial low-voltage markets including building automation, fire alarm, security, voice and data, and lighting controls. The company also supports emerging sectors such as battery energy storage systems (BESS) and AI infrastructure fiber deployments. Its client base includes contractors like Automated Controls and government agencies through its approved-vendor status.

The company differentiates itself through a "Customer First" mantra, a commitment to sourcing only from certified manufacturers, and a dedicated team of industry veterans with decades of experience. Its stated mission is to deliver the right wire and cable when needed, backed by a promise of high-quality, certified products and responsive, knowledgeable service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire and cable distribution", "Warehousing and logistics", "Same-day shipping", "Customized cable solutions", "Government procurement support", "Mil-Spec cable supply", "Aerospace cable supply", "Shipboard cable supply", "Low-voltage cable supply", "Technical product selection assistance"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Shipboard/Marine", "Defense/Military (Mil-Spec)", "Building automation", "Fire alarm and life safety", "Security systems", "Voice and data communications", "Lighting controls", "Battery energy storage systems (BESS)", "AI infrastructure"], "materials": ["Service entrance cable", "Duplex service drop cable", "Quadruplex service drop cable", "Triplex service drop cable", "Multi-conductor cable", "Control and automation cable", "Life safety cable", "Fiber optic cable", "Mil-Spec cable", "Shipboard cable", "Low-voltage cable"], "equipment": [], "volume": "300 million feet per year", "lead_time": "Same-day service for stocked items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day service on stocked items", "Government-approved vendor for Mil-Spec, aerospace, and shipboard cables", "Sources exclusively from certified manufacturers", "Distributes over 300 million feet of wire per year", "Team with over 20 years of industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 in Richardson, Texas by Joe Stadelman -> /about", "Distributes over 300 million feet of wire annually -> /about", "Same-day service on stocked items -> / and /about", "Government-approved vendor for Mil-Spec, aerospace, and shipboard cables -> /about", "Sources exclusively from certified manufacturers -> /about", "Serves aerospace, shipboard, defense, low-voltage, building automation, fire alarm, security, voice/data, lighting controls -> /about and team bios", "Customer example: Automated Controls -> / (homepage testimonial)", "Warehouse in Dallas, TX -> /about (Alex Alejandre oversees warehouse in Dallas, TX)", "Team includes industry veterans with 20+ years experience -> /about", "Product categories: Service entrance, duplex/quadruplex/triplex service drop, multi-conductor, controls & automation, life safety -> / (homepage) and capabilities", "Volume: 1000+ satisfied customers, 100,000+ completed projects per year -> /about", "Mission: help get right wire and cable when needed -> /about", "Vision: become nation''s number one commercial wire and cable distributor -> /about", "Brand values: Efficient, Reliable, Agile, High-Quality, Dedicated Experts -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Your Wire & Cable Distributor", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='best-wire-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bethlehem Wire Rope, Inc. traces its origins to 1886 in Williamsport, Pennsylvania, where it began supplying structural strength wire rope, cable, and strand. Today the company operates a 46-acre manufacturing complex with more than 620,000 square feet under roof, which it describes as the single largest wire rope manufacturing facility in North America.

The vertically integrated plant produces its own wire, closes rope, forms structural strand, and fabricates finished assemblies such as pendants and other fittings on the same premises. The product range covers general-purpose wire rope, surface and underground mining ropes, drilling and service rig cables for offshore oil and gas, elevator hoist cables, boom pendants for lifting and rigging, structural strand for bridges, and specialty ropes for ski lifts, logging, and marine environments.

Customers span construction, logging, marine, mining, oil and gas, and steel industries. Typical applications include crane and elevator hoisting, bridge suspension and anchoring, and offshore platform stabilization.

